INVARIANTS ENFORCED
-------------------
1. Epoch Isolation: Cache keys MUST include epoch ID
   - Violation: Cache hit from different epoch
   - Guard: resourceGuards_.epochId in cache key

2. Fact Count Bound: Total facts ≤ MaxFactCount
   - Violation: Fact explosion in recursive rules
   - Guard: FactCountTracker throws on limit exceeded

3. Time Bound: Execution time ≤ MaxRuleTime
   - Violation: Infinite loop or excessive computation
   - Guard: RuleExecutionTimer throws on timeout

4. Memory Bound: Heap growth ≤ MaxMemory
   - Violation: OOM during rule execution
   - Guard: MemoryUsageTracker throws on limit exceeded

5. Manifest Determinism: Cache keys include manifest hash
   - Violation: Stale cache hit across different data versions
   - Guard: manifestHash in cache key

INTEGRATION POINTS
------------------
1. QueryExecutionContext
   - Provides currentEpochId_ (uint64_t)
   - Provides boundEpochManifest_ (optional<EpochManifest>)
   - Provides getEpochDeterministicKey() (manifest hash)

2. EpochManifest
   - Provides getManifestHash() (SHA-256 of all fields)
   - Computed once at index load time
   - Immutable during epoch SERVE state

3. AllocatorWithLimit
   - Tracks memory allocations
   - Used by MemoryUsageTracker for accurate heap monitoring

4. Operation base class
   - getCacheKeyImpl() virtual method
   - Overridden to include epoch ID in Datalog operations

BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY
----------------------
- Non-breaking: Existing Datalog operations continue to work
- Cache invalidation: Existing cache entries without epoch ID are ignored
- Migration: No manual migration required (automatic via cache key mismatch)

PERFORMANCE IMPACT
------------------
- Cache key computation: +2 string concatenations (epoch ID, manifest hash)
- Runtime overhead: ~1-2% for cache key generation
- Resource tracking: ~5-10% overhead during rule execution
- Memory overhead: 3 tracker objects per FixpointComputation (~100 bytes)

FAILURE MODES
-------------
1. Fact count limit exceeded
   - Exception: ResourceGuardViolation
   - Message: "Fact count limit exceeded: <count> > <limit>"
   - Recovery: Reduce rule complexity or increase maxFactCount

2. Time limit exceeded
   - Exception: ResourceGuardViolation
   - Message: "Rule execution time limit exceeded: <time>ms > <limit>ms"
   - Recovery: Optimize rule or increase maxRuleTime

3. Memory limit exceeded
   - Exception: ResourceGuardViolation
   - Message: "Memory limit exceeded: <usage> > <limit>"
   - Recovery: Reduce data size or increase maxMemoryBytes

